        {
          "id": "qss_step250_row23_col25_enhanced_melting",
          "description": "Same reference chain, regime and tolerance reasoning as qss_step250_row23_col24_mixed_phase_accretion, one tile column to the east (i = 25): the layer just above freezing (layer 8, T = 273.3 K) holds snow, graupel, rain and cloud water at once, so both enhanced-melting terms pseml (1.3e-15) and pgeml (1.7e-14 kg/kg/s) are active and unlimited there, together with the above-freezing accretions psacw, pgacw, psacr and pgacr that feed them. Measured residual <= 6e-8 of column maximum in every accretion rate; pseml and pgeml differ by 1.6e-5 relative because they multiply the supercooling T0 - T = -0.15 K, where the kernel's real32 T0 (273.1499939 K) is 6e-6 K off, hence rel 5e-5 / Linf 1e-4 of column maximum for those two.",
